  "uprn": "100021558653",
  "decision_date": "13/07/2004",
  "description": "Erection of a single storey rear extension to No 33 and conversion of properties into one single dwellinghouse",
  "site_name": "33-35",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "15/07/2004",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW4 7JQ",
  "street_name": "Rosemary Avenue",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "12/07/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - It is considered that the erection of a single-storey rear extension to number 33 Rosemary Avenue and conversion of the properties into one single-family dwellinghouse, would be acceptable having due regard for the site characteristics of 33 and 35 Rosemary Avenue, and would be compatible with the character and appearance of the locality, and would not harm the living conditions of the occupiers or adjoining occupiers, or result in conditions prejudicial to highway safety. The development is therefore in accordance with Unitary Development Plan policies (Adopted December 2003) ENV-B.1.1, H.4.1, H.6.4 and T.1.4. and the Council's Residential Guidelines (July 2002).",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the extension is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing single-storey rear extension at number 35 Rosemary Avenue.",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the east and west walls of the extension hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - No part of the roof of the extension shall be used as or altered to form a balcony, roof garden or similar amenity area.",
    "Condition : 7 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out."
  ],
